    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` (e.g. `'SMI-0007-M26'`), where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince the membership number is derived purely from two fields already stored on the owner (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), I computed it on read rather than persisting a redundant column \u2014 mirroring how the existing derived fields `displayName` and `initials` are handled in the mapper. Two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto` plus a helper:\n   ```java\n   default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {\n       if (owner == null || owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {\n           return null;\n       }\n       return String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);\n   }\n   ```\n   The `%02d` on `year % 100` guarantees the two-digit `YY` (zero-padded).\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` checkpoint, which derives the expected value from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, now passes).",
